 *> Implementation test of the pose of another player on the client (T6202; docs/protocol/53 sections 1 and 10, 12 section 7.5, 34-2 crouching):
*> Set Entity Data entry 0 (BYTE, shared flags) and entry 6 (POSE) are kept in the replica row; a player in the crouching pose (5) is drawn
*> crouched (head and body lowered: 12 section 7.5 head y + 4.2 pixels), so the top of the model is lower than a standing one.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-POSE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CLMODELS.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-PLAYER-ID           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-AREA            PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FLAGS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POSE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FIRST               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LAST                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RANGE.
    05 WS-R                BINARY-LONG OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 01 WS-TOP-STAND           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TOP-CROUCH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EYE-TABLE.
    05 WS-EYE              FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO PK-COUNT
     CALL "ENTITY-ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 256 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO SK-U PL-YAW
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EYE(1) WS-EYE(3)
     MOVE 64 TO WS-EYE(2)
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "player" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-PLAYER-ID WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-X
     MOVE 64 TO WS-Y
     MOVE 12.5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "EPO-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-PLAYER-ID WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "EPO-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE WS-R(4) TO WS-TOP-STAND
     MOVE "entity pose a standing player is drawn (its vertices exist)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF RL-EN-COUNT > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE 2 TO WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 5 TO WS-POSE
     CALL "EPO-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS WS-POSE
     MOVE "entity pose Set Entity Data entry 6 keeps the pose (5)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-POSE(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "entity pose Set Entity Data entry 0 keeps the flags byte (2)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-FLAGS(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "EPO-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE WS-R(4) TO WS-TOP-CROUCH
     MOVE "entity pose a crouching player's model is lower than a standing one (more than 0.1 block)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-TOP-STAND - WS-TOP-CROUCH > 100
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Swimming (pose 3, flags 0x18): the swim amount rises 0.09 a tick to 1 in 12 ticks (53 section 12), the body turns to lie flat about the pivot
*>   (13: rotation -90 about X, translation (0, -1, 0.3)): the top of the model is then under 1 block above the feet (head top 0.3 + 0.234 x 0.9375
*>   at most), against 1.8 standing; crawling (pose 3, flag clear) is the same.
     MOVE 24 TO WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 3 TO WS-POSE
     CALL "EPO-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS WS-POSE
     PERFORM 5 TIMES
         CALL "ENTITIES-SWIM-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "entity pose five ticks of swimming give a swim amount of 0.45" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 450 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = EN-SWIM(1) * 1000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM 7 TIMES
         CALL "ENTITIES-SWIM-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "entity pose twelve ticks of swimming give a swim amount of 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1000 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = EN-SWIM(1) * 1000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "EPO-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE "entity pose a swimming player lies flat: the model's top is under 1 block above its feet" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-R(4) < 1000
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-POSE
     CALL "EPO-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS WS-POSE
     PERFORM 13 TIMES
         CALL "ENTITIES-SWIM-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "entity pose a standing player's swim amount falls back to 0 in 12 ticks" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = EN-SWIM(1) * 1000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-POSE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EPO-DATA.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, flags, pose: Set Entity Data with entry 0 (BYTE) and entry 6 (POSE).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==MD-==.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-DATA                BINARY-LONG VALUE 101.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-FLAGS                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-POSE                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-FLAGS L-POSE.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 0 TO MD-MD-INDEX
     MOVE MD-MDS-BYTE TO MD-MD-SERIALIZER
     MOVE L-FLAGS TO MD-MD-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 6 TO MD-MD-INDEX
     MOVE MD-MDS-POSE TO MD-MD-SERIALIZER
     MOVE L-POSE TO MD-MD-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE MD-MD-END TO MD-MD-INDEX
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-DATA
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EPO-DATA.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EPO-SPAWN.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, type (registry id), x y z (FLOAT-LONG): Add Entity at rest.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-ADD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-V0                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V1                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V2                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-A0                  FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-TYPE L-X L-Y L-Z.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER WS-V0 WS-V1 WS-V2
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-ADD
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EPO-SPAWN.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EPO-RANGE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, first and last entity vertex, range out (BINARY-LONG x 6): min and max x, y, z in thousandths.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-V                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-FIRST                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-LAST                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RANGE.
    05 L-R                 BINARY-LONG OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-FIRST L-LAST L-RANGE.
     MOVE 999999999 TO L-R(1) L-R(3) L-R(5)
     MOVE -999999999 TO L-R(2) L-R(4) L-R(6)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM L-FIRST BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > L-LAST
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-X(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(1), WS-V) TO L-R(1)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(2), WS-V) TO L-R(2)
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-Y(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(3), WS-V) TO L-R(3)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(4), WS-V) TO L-R(4)
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-Z(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(5), WS-V) TO L-R(5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(6), WS-V) TO L-R(6)
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EPO-RANGE.
